                <pb facs="hu_d14-1" n="1" xml:id="ni_d14-1"/>

                <head>NI–14. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On May 31 and June 1, a group of approximately fifty Nicaraguan exiles from Costa
                    Rica launched an invasion in the hill country of central Nicaragua. At the
                    request of the Nicaraguan Ambassador, Sevilla-Sacasa, the Organization of American States met in
                    Washington on June 2. <pb facs="0949" n="861" type="typeset" xml:id="pg861"/> On
                    June 4, the OAS approved sending a fact-finding
                    mission to report on the situation. Neither the Nicaraguan Ambassador nor
                    President Somoza formally charged the Costa Rican Government with complicity in
                    the invasion, but instead levelled charges against the Government of Cuba. By
                    June 12, after several engagements with the Nicaraguan National Guard, the
                    invaders either surrendered or were isolated and driven into the jungle.
                    Documentation on the invasion attempt is in file 717.00. The text of the OAS resolution on Nicaragua is printed in the
                    Department of State <hi rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, July 6, 1959, pp.
                    30–32.</p>
            </div>
